      "worked": "The variable base requires $x>0$ and $x\\ne1$. Let $u=\\log_2 x$, so $u\\ne0$. By change of base,\n\n$$\\log_x2=\\frac{\\log_2 2}{\\log_2 x}=\\frac1u.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}u+\\frac1u&=4\\\\u^2-4u+1&=0\\\\(u-2)^2&=3\\\\u&=2\\pm\\sqrt3\\\\x&=2^{2\\pm\\sqrt3}\\end{align*}$$\n\nBoth exponents are nonzero, so both positive values satisfy the base restrictions.",
